{"data":{"title":"His Name Is Mutty Ranks","slug":"his-name-is-mutty-ranks","path":"/artists/a-tribe-called-quest/tracks/his-name-is-mutty-ranks/","artwork":"images/artists/a-tribe-called-quest/tracks/his-name-is-mutty-ranks.jpg","artist":{"id":"j7kamL8aLZo","slug":"a-tribe-called-quest","links":null,"title":"A Tribe Called Quest","artwork":null},"id":"LPo4dbsXa0U"},"appearanceCount":3,"markers":[{"chapter":{"id":"qoj5IS3WuCk","show":{"id":"vPfL7UzxY4Y","slug":"139","title":"Soulection Radio Show #139 w/ DJ Harrison","artwork":"/images/episodes/139.jpg","content":"DJ Harrison thows down a crazy live improvised session with the SP-404 and MPC1000\n\n<!--more-->\n\noe Kay started off with some nice deep/melodic tracks from Mr. Carmack, Christoph El Truento, Dirg Gerner, Iamnobodi, Sango, Last Night In Paris, Geode and many more! Joe took it back to the essence with Ginuwine/Timbaland/Dilla classics! DJ Harrison on the other hand who reminds us of Madlib (no really he does)all the way from Virginia threw down a crazy live session with the SP-404 & MPC 1000. Lots of soulful chops and intricate drum patterns! This is another amazing session from start to finish! Spread this if you feel it.\n\nThanks to [true listener^^](https://soundcloud.com/true_listener) for supplying this tracklist.\n","published_at":"2013-08-03T00:00:00+00:00"}}},{"chapter":{"id":"XpE941A1_VQ","show":{"id":"cgQYpogYRzc","slug":"204","title":"Soulection Radio Show #204 (Dilla Tribute)","artwork":"/images/episodes/204.jpg","content":"\n<!--more-->\n\n","published_at":"2015-02-08T00:00:00+00:00"}}},{"chapter":{"id":"k5TgGkYDGyk","show":{"id":"XGAYE5T-iO0","slug":"252","title":"Soulection Radio Show #252 (Phife Dawg Tribute)","artwork":"/images/episodes/252.jpg","content":"\n<!--more-->\n\n","published_at":"2016-03-26T00:00:00+00:00"}}}],"linkedPlatforms":[{"id":40756,"platform":"youtube","href":"https://music.youtube.com/watch?v=pvor2P7dNtU","artwork":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/pvor2P7dNtU/hqdefault.jpg",